{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549669-warlock-the-pretension-april-fools-day-book","id":1549669,"title":"Warlock: the Pretension (April Fools Day book)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-03-31T08:24:53-07:00","id":1549669,"title":"Warlock: the Pretension (April Fools Day book)","content":"<a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/513111/Warlock-The-Pretension-Black-Dog-Gaming-Magazine-Presents\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/pr...azine-Presents</a><br /> <br /> So I made a new Storytellers Vault Book for April Fools. It's a fleshing out of the in-universe Black Dog Game Factory game, Warlock: the Pretension. It's 160 pages full of new factions and dumb jokes. I've been working on it for half with feedback from Storytellers Vault community, so I hope people enjoy it. Happy April Fool days, everyone!<br /> <br /> P S. As an update on my Modern Crafts project, it hit some development delays and its release wasn't time sensitive like this was, so I put it on the back burner. I intend to release two volumes of it together later this year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-23T12:17:54-07:00","id":1550343,"title":"","content":"I apologise for taking so long to post a reply here, but I tend to frequent the VAMPIRE and WEREWOLF board because I have only a passing acquaintance with the other lines.<br /> <br /> I do, however, know enough about Black Dog to be delighted by this de-fictionalisation of a game line: heck, I\u2019d love to discuss the challenge of working out how to balance the clear parody of White Wolf games against the desire to make the game sound like something a gamer would actually play.<br /> <br /> Well, that and fudging details enough so that the various Ancient Conspiracies don\u2019t squash you like a bug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-23T17:52:48-07:00","id":1550353,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately the current exchange rate USD/BRL is still prohibitive for me even at this price. For now, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-24T08:26:06-07:00","id":1550361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549669-warlock-the-pretension-april-fools-day-book?p=1550343#post1550343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I apologise for taking so long to post a reply here, but I tend to frequent the VAMPIRE and WEREWOLF board because I have only a passing acquaintance with the other lines.<br /> <br /> I do, however, know enough about Black Dog to be delighted by this de-fictionalisation of a game line: heck, I\u2019d love to discuss the challenge of working out how to balance the clear parody of White Wolf games against the desire to make the game sound like something a gamer would actually play.<br /> <br /> Well, that and fudging details enough so that the various Ancient Conspiracies don\u2019t squash you like a bug.</div> </div> </div> </div>It helped that I was getting feedback from the Storytellers Vault community. The whole magazine format was one of their suggestions. That let me expand to parodying an entire hypothetical edition of Warlock, while not waste words recreating basic rules and whatnot that the veteran Mage readers that would likely buy the book could substitute existing Mage content in for.<br /> <br /> I also jumped on White Wolf changing ownership repeatedly to try and decouple Black Dog from explicitly being a Pentex subsidiary. It can be still, but I left that up to Storytellers/Tailspinners. I wanted this to be a more Mage like interpretation of Black Dog, so went in a different, more Marauder-y direction, of what was going on behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> In terms of the different factions, a key guideline in my head was I wanted them to be parody the existing ones groups while still being able to stand apart from them. If you couldn't pluck them out of Warlock and put them alongside their Mage counterpart and they still work as separate entities, I felt that would be leaning too much into parody for parody sake. Take the Bloody Fist for example. Obviously they are meant to be the Akashayana spoof, but they are also completely different, being a play on MMA/Bloodsport/Mortal Kombat/Tournament fighter media. <br /> <br /> This did result in me scrapping some early ideas. One early concept was Society of Ether parody that was just Flat Earthers. Ultimately, I decided this was just a one note joke version Society of Ether, and switched it out with Haunt Hunters, which I felt was a lot more interesting to play with, combining a different kind of fringe weird science from Etherites with the whole libertarian public services vibe of Ghostbusters and the behind the scenes drama involving different IPs with the same name.<br /> <br /> Anything more specific anyone was interested in hearing about the dev process?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-25T04:33:54-07:00","id":1550376,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll have to read the whole thing before going into more detail, but would like to thank you for taking the time to reply, as well as compliment you once again for putting all this together.<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m wondering if there could be a schism within Black Dog resulting in various game designers haring off with their own special little interests and creating little sub-worlds out of them (As a way of explaining, for example, why LYCANTHROPE would remain very firmly wedded to Pentex*, whilst REVENANT gets slightly less psychotic, much more respectable).<br /> <br /> Also, I\u2019m stone-cold certain that the interpersonal drama at Black Dog is one of the few times an RPG creator wouod inspire more than one episode of True Crime programming\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}